<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell July 20-22 Bombay naphtha.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell July 20-22 Bombay naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has offered by tender 25,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) lifting July 20-22 from Bombay on the west coast, industry sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>The tender closes July 10 and is valid until July 11.</p>
<p>IOC's last LAN cargo from Bombay lifting June 17-19 was awarded at $16.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
